#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119647 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119933 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b02f02f1-f270-55e0-a7a9-0b729c4d82c0" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equation of the Plane Parallel To Two Given Vectors"}] :question/id #uuid "a6fded96-287a-53ee-8b1c-dd618562b2c2" :question/math-academy-id "e-4940" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(-3,2,5)$ and is parallel to the vectors $\\mathbf{b}= \\langle 17,3,15 \\rangle$  and $\\mathbf{c}= \\langle 5,0,-8 \\rangle.$" :question/worked-solution "A parametric equation of a plane is given by \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}=\\mathbf{p}+ s\\mathbf{b}+ t \\mathbf{c},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{p}$ is the position vector of a point on the plane and the vectors $\\mathbf{b}$ and $\\mathbf{c}$ are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nHere, the position vector of the given point $P$ is $\\mathbf{p}=\\langle -3,2,5 \\rangle,$ and the two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other) are $\\mathbf{b}= \\langle 17,3,15 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{c}= \\langle 5,0,-8 \\rangle.$\n\nSo, a parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =⟨-3,2,5⟩+s\\,⟨17,3,15⟩+t\\,⟨5,0,-8⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119648 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119935 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3061cb06-f57f-57c8-8821-dbd962b1e78e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equation of the Plane Parallel To Two Lines"}] :question/id #uuid "297bda8f-6e33-5cc2-a2e1-5ab6186fa9d0" :question/math-academy-id "e-4941" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $C(2,50,-19)$ and is parallel to the lines $\\mathbf{r}= \\langle 2,\\sqrt{6},17 \\rangle + s \\langle -1,7,2 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{r}= \\langle 20,-44, 27 \\rangle + t \\langle 2\\sqrt{3},9,-8 \\rangle$." :question/worked-solution "The direction vectors of the lines are $\\mathbf{v_1}=\\langle  -1,7,2  \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{v_2}=\\langle 2\\sqrt{3},9,-8 \\rangle$, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $C(2,50,-19)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $\\mathbf{c}=\\langle 2,50,-19 \\rangle.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =c+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨2,50,-19⟩+s\\,⟨-1,7,2⟩+t\\,⟨2\\sqrt{3},9,-8⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119649 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119936 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d11f13f0-1cfa-59ec-a04a-9483d942b1aa" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equation of the Plane Passing Through Three Given Points"}] :question/id #uuid "9c36ddd5-fcf1-5c4d-a350-aa8ef3a3ca9e" :question/math-academy-id "e-4942" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the points $A(-1,4,-3),$ $B(7,5,4),$ and $C(2,-2,8).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other). Let's use the displacement vectors $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨7,5,4⟩-⟨-1,4,-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8,1,7⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =⟨2,-2,8⟩-⟨-1,4,-3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,-6,11⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, if we consider the position vector $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle -1,4,-3 \\rangle$ of the point $A,$ then the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =a+s\\overset{\\to }{AB}+t\\overset{\\to }{AC} \\\\ r & =⟨-1,4,-3⟩+s⟨8,1,7⟩+t⟨3,-6,11⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Watch out!** The form of the final equation depends on our choice of vectors and the point on the plane. We could have picked other vectors. Likewise, we could have chosen $B$ or $C$ instead of $A$ as our point on the plane. So, the answer is *not unique*!"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119664 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119934 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "62196ae9-df2e-5a3a-bc0a-1c0f4c40af3e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Normal Vector To a Plane Given by Parametric Equation"}] :question/id #uuid "b86eace4-01cb-5601-8e9b-2658e81fc656" :question/math-academy-id "e-5884" :question/problem "Find a normal vector to the plane \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}= \\langle -6,3, 2 \\rangle + t \\langle 4, 2, -1 \\rangle + s \\langle 4, -3, 2 \\rangle,\\qquad t,\\,s \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the parametric equation, we have that $\\mathbf{v} = \\langle 4, 2, -1 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{w} = \\langle 4, -3, 2 \\rangle$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $\\mathbf{v}$ and $\\mathbf{w}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =i-12j-20k \\\\  & =⟨1,-12,-20⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $\\mathbf{n}=\\langle 1, -12, -20 \\rangle.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262916 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119934 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "62196ae9-df2e-5a3a-bc0a-1c0f4c40af3e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Normal Vector To a Plane Given by Parametric Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b4a3c41-2d3e-5406-a2cd-cbab49cb529e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨6,-4,-26⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260257} {:answer/id #uuid "63d710f5-99cb-53b4-8290-6299023ee722" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨8,-2,17⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260737} {:answer/id #uuid "95c11743-7580-55cc-a7f1-587f795b6ee6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-8,-2,-22⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261175} {:answer/id #uuid "9e1ed729-7d24-5fef-a919-3b87d20a7b2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-8,2,-11⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261244} {:answer/id #uuid "da606c57-af3e-52fa-9552-99fdba561ef0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,-8,-7⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261803}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95c11743-7580-55cc-a7f1-587f795b6ee6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-8,-2,-22⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261175} :answer-field/id #uuid "e859b94c-82b3-57fc-b159-f1a0791b5216" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262532}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "58d7da64-39e5-5263-82e1-d46d43bc9c9d" :question/math-academy-id "q-128497" :question/problem "Find a normal vector to the plane\n\n$$\nr=⟨3,\\sqrt{7},-2⟩+t⟨-2,8,0⟩+s⟨3,-1,-1⟩,\\,t,\\,s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨-2,8,0⟩$ and $w=⟨3,-1,-1⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -2 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-8i-2j-22k \\\\  & =⟨-8,-2,-22⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨-8,-2,-22⟩.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186387887 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119935 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3061cb06-f57f-57c8-8821-dbd962b1e78e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equation of the Plane Parallel To Two Lines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7bcab70b-517a-5271-894e-c4b561597fd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨3,-2,7⟩+s⟨3,-1,5⟩+t⟨3,6,7⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387889} {:answer/id #uuid "4a4c8236-4299-5664-9863-74ff3a24010c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨7,2,3⟩+s⟨2,-1,2⟩+t⟨4,3,7⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387890} {:answer/id #uuid "37f487f1-ec69-5071-83c4-95ce287eda90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨2,-7,3⟩+s⟨2,-4,1⟩+t⟨3,5,2⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387891} {:answer/id #uuid "46c96bf2-16f7-52a0-a229-e72577f23ffd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨7,-2,3⟩+s⟨2,-2,1⟩+t⟨3,4,7⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387892} {:answer/id #uuid "03dc462d-3599-5fba-aad0-834967006884" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨7,-3,2⟩+s⟨3,-2,1⟩+t⟨7,4,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387893}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46c96bf2-16f7-52a0-a229-e72577f23ffd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨7,-2,3⟩+s⟨2,-2,1⟩+t⟨3,4,7⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387892} :answer-field/id #uuid "99d29468-156d-5427-b6e3-354339252a04" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186387888}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6d8e167e-ba7b-5746-8896-10f0f88087c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-128501" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $A(7,-2,3)$ and is parallel to the lines $r=⟨9,2,1⟩+s⟨2,-2,1⟩$ and $r=⟨4,-5,19⟩+t⟨3,4,7⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=⟨2,-2,1⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨3,4,7⟩$, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $A(7,-2,3)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $a=⟨7,-2,3⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =a+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨7,-2,3⟩+s⟨2,-2,1⟩+t⟨3,4,7⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120234 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119933 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b02f02f1-f270-55e0-a7a9-0b729c4d82c0" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equation of the Plane Parallel To Two Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "941f6bb6-ca0b-5ea1-b87c-af2fa80d4876" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r = ⟨0, 2,-0.5⟩ + s⟨1, 3, 0⟩ + t⟨1,-1, 3⟩, s, t ∈ (- ∞, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117564} {:answer/id #uuid "986efc18-be18-5b16-b8b4-99fc183d1672" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117565} {:answer/id #uuid "1395bc4f-e4f7-5963-be28-263b9823d510" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r = ⟨1,-1, 3⟩ + s⟨1, 3, 0⟩ + t⟨0, 2,-0.5⟩, s, t ∈ (- ∞, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117566} {:answer/id #uuid "5fdc530d-3b00-5f5d-8bc0-018659ce8625" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r = s⟨1, 3, 0⟩ + t⟨0, 2,-0.5⟩, s, t ∈ (- ∞, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117567} {:answer/id #uuid "643bbf8e-a5ac-5da5-8c23-895f54546f79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r = ⟨1, 3, 0⟩ + s⟨1,-1, 3⟩ + t⟨0, 2,-0.5⟩, s, t ∈ (- ∞, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117568}] :answer-field/id #uuid "de75ec3a-0ae7-5e53-b679-aa489a6e2938" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117563}] :question/id #uuid "001b7edd-c428-5436-8d89-3502541770a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-33154" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(1,-1, 3)$ and is parallel to the vectors $v_{1} = ⟨1, 3, 0⟩$ and $v_{2} = ⟨0, 2,-0.5⟩$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120236 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119935 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3061cb06-f57f-57c8-8821-dbd962b1e78e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equation of the Plane Parallel To Two Lines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2646d87e-2e74-5757-bc34-02f20d6114fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-2,23,14⟩+s⟨-3,5,4⟩+t⟨4,7,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302705} {:answer/id #uuid "5ff6b838-1af4-5c00-868a-734468c82814" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-2,23,14⟩+s⟨-3,5,1⟩+t⟨-30,55,25⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303040} {:answer/id #uuid "68558628-ae8a-519a-9cf8-9a1b1e7f6286" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The plane is undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303091} {:answer/id #uuid "c6a9c33e-fe94-5b43-8ee0-a43a2a47c5eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-2,23,14⟩+s⟨-3,5,1⟩+t⟨4,7,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303676} {:answer/id #uuid "e74734b6-d893-59de-a060-0512213f4bdd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-3,5,4⟩+s⟨-2,23,14⟩+t⟨4,7,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303894}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2646d87e-2e74-5757-bc34-02f20d6114fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-2,23,14⟩+s⟨-3,5,4⟩+t⟨4,7,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302705} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8f249d4-cd35-55dd-9318-5acc4887eb5e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304576}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "88872368-686b-5e7f-9016-e33ff5ee0ad5" :question/math-academy-id "q-33158" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $B(-2,23,14)$ and is parallel to the lines $r=⟨-3,5,1⟩+s⟨-3,5,4⟩$ and $r=⟨-30,55,25⟩+t⟨4,7,-1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=⟨-3,5,4⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨4,7,-1⟩$, respectively. These vectors are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nWe also know that the point $B(-2,23,14)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $b=⟨-2,23,14⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =b+s{v}_{1}+t{v}_{2} \\\\ r & =⟨-2,23,14⟩+s⟨-3,5,4⟩+t⟨4,7,-1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304926 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119936 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d11f13f0-1cfa-59ec-a04a-9483d942b1aa" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equation of the Plane Passing Through Three Given Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "336bb496-d1df-5e9a-a07a-1ec951355ede" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The plane is undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302774} {:answer/id #uuid "8e8dad69-2acf-5472-9a3f-505a95ac3fea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨-2,-2,-2⟩+s⟨1,4,-14⟩+t⟨1,1,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303341} {:answer/id #uuid "b208b020-2e95-5012-90d1-880d0704ce1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,4,-14⟩+s⟨-2,-2,-2⟩+t⟨1,1,1⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303557} {:answer/id #uuid "d3a6125d-748b-50ac-93e6-06be995d0638" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨0,3,-19⟩+s⟨-2,-2,-2⟩+t⟨1,2,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303769} {:answer/id #uuid "feb8b07e-b16f-57b2-afdf-a8e6076cfea6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,4,-14⟩+s⟨1,1,1⟩+t⟨1,-2,-26⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304058}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "feb8b07e-b16f-57b2-afdf-a8e6076cfea6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,4,-14⟩+s⟨1,1,1⟩+t⟨1,-2,-26⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304058} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a308e92-1035-59ed-9244-1f44706e0efe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304233}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "133e1de3-de48-5298-8948-a57726f1d155" :question/math-academy-id "q-33160" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $C(1,4,-14)$ and is parallel to the two distinct lines $r=⟨-1,5,7⟩+s⟨1,1,1⟩$ and $r=⟨0,3,-19⟩+t⟨-2,-2,-2⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The direction vectors of the lines are ${v}_{1}=⟨-2,-2,-2⟩$ and ${v}_{2}=⟨1,1,1⟩,$ respectively.\nBut ${v}_{2}=-2{v}_{1}.$ So, our lines are parallel. \n\nDespite this fact, two distinct parallel lines still determine a plane. Now: \n\n- from the equation of the first line, we get the point $P$ with the position vector $p=⟨-1,5,7⟩$ that lies on it, and\n\n- from the equation of the second line, we get the point $Q$ with the position vector $q=⟨0,3,-19⟩$ that lies on it.\n\nThe vector $u=q-p$ will be parallel to the required plane. \n\nComputing the coordinates of $u,$  we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =q-p \\\\  & =⟨0,3,-19⟩-⟨-1,5,7⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-2,-26⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}∦{v}_{1},$ we can find the equation of our plane.\n\nWe know that the point $C(1,4,-14)$ lies on the plane and its position vector is $c=⟨1,4,-14⟩.$  \n\nSo, the corresponding parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =c+s{v}_{1}+tu \\\\ r & =⟨1,4,-14⟩+s⟨1,1,1⟩+t⟨1,-2,-26⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120278 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119934 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "62196ae9-df2e-5a3a-bc0a-1c0f4c40af3e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Normal Vector To a Plane Given by Parametric Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11b5e92d-6224-56f5-944e-a8b83ad251a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-59,10,-20⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308877} {:answer/id #uuid "719fd09d-d078-59ed-81b8-c5e456b9a391" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-95,20,-10⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309632} {:answer/id #uuid "740f86a3-b4cf-5219-84a0-d82570a20efd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,0,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309648} {:answer/id #uuid "90ffb081-cc79-57a0-a759-a970dcf68248" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-4,-84,25⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309908} {:answer/id #uuid "b018f396-0291-53b4-b697-3ecdf0cb89a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,-7,5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310170}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "719fd09d-d078-59ed-81b8-c5e456b9a391" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-95,20,-10⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309632} :answer-field/id #uuid "121b2d9e-6258-5ba0-b2c8-a9ee055f9a6e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310841}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "183d75ab-bc55-5284-9356-4879f8cd6310" :question/math-academy-id "q-33818" :question/problem "Find a normal vector to the plane\n\n$$\nr=⟨2,0,-1⟩+t⟨-2,-7,5⟩+s⟨2,12,5⟩,\\,t,\\,s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨-2,-7,5⟩$ and $w=⟨2,12,5⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -2 & -7 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 12 & 5\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-95i+20j-10k \\\\  & =⟨-95,20,-10⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨-95,20,-10⟩.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391682 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119934 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "62196ae9-df2e-5a3a-bc0a-1c0f4c40af3e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Normal Vector To a Plane Given by Parametric Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23e02ac0-3e89-5c73-aee7-9f2de3148d7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,2,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391684} {:answer/id #uuid "8ffc566d-8d4c-53c3-af4b-b2d7a4d35946" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,1,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391685} {:answer/id #uuid "efc39529-4f0f-5e00-b796-0c632007c03e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2,0,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391686} {:answer/id #uuid "f83846d5-42d7-540e-ad5c-05350b13e9fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-2,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391687} {:answer/id #uuid "0693f405-c3d1-5022-a785-4b3d44119374" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,1,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391688}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23e02ac0-3e89-5c73-aee7-9f2de3148d7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,2,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391684} :answer-field/id #uuid "8aebbae6-4b97-5e3f-9a17-15682100023d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391683}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3b07ac22-3309-5bc0-ac4b-6e1be0e5a45e" :question/math-academy-id "q-33823" :question/problem "Find a normal vector to the plane\n\n$$\nr=⟨1,1,0⟩+t⟨-1,1,1⟩+s⟨0,2,2⟩,\\,t,\\,s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨-1,1,1⟩$ and $w=⟨0,2,2⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =2j-2k \\\\  & =⟨0,2,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨0,2,-2⟩.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338860 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119933 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b02f02f1-f270-55e0-a7a9-0b729c4d82c0" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equation of the Plane Parallel To Two Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a61a21b-5fdc-504b-85e6-efa8045c017b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0.25\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336276} {:answer/id #uuid "251c8495-3b53-53ba-b0bb-117ca0f25022" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0.25\\end{aligned}],\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336380} {:answer/id #uuid "32bc3ffa-f9fc-57fb-b002-3f769687d521" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336513} {:answer/id #uuid "bc7025e4-5c0f-5f75-ac1f-2f454bf34e82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=s[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0.25\\end{aligned}],\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337705} {:answer/id #uuid "e7333efd-0842-52ba-960c-8e72d761ec4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0.25\\end{aligned}],\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338052}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "251c8495-3b53-53ba-b0bb-117ca0f25022" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0.25\\end{aligned}],\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336380} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee208f77-0c4b-5286-8089-ce9b7fe1a2f9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338694}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "45799451-d7b1-5abf-840c-3d93dcdaeb60" :question/math-academy-id "q-70969" :question/problem "Find a parametric equation of the plane that passes through the point $T(7,0,-3)$ and is parallel to the vectors ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$  and ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0.25\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "A parametric equation of a plane is given by \n\n$$\nr=p+sb+tc,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is the position vector of a point on the plane and the vectors $b$ and $c$ are parallel to the plane but not to each other.\n\nHere, the position vector of the given point $T$ is $p=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$, and the two vectors that are parallel to the plane (but not to each other) are ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$  and ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0.25\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSo, a parametric equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0.25\\end{aligned}],\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338863 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119934 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "62196ae9-df2e-5a3a-bc0a-1c0f4c40af3e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Normal Vector To a Plane Given by Parametric Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13372795-1d9c-59ee-ba7f-59bbde3f9d61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,0,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336213} {:answer/id #uuid "14870064-b7e8-54d0-99ca-4b64bfe2bd62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,0,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336226} {:answer/id #uuid "2c7f5521-fd3a-51c7-9ecf-a3af94ee1454" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,-1,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336454} {:answer/id #uuid "6249715c-fc3f-56fb-9993-32d1a515b62a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,0,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336915} {:answer/id #uuid "c671655c-abd1-563c-aef5-4ee4cece1841" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,1,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337791}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c671655c-abd1-563c-aef5-4ee4cece1841" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨4,1,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337791} :answer-field/id #uuid "be9468de-a381-56af-b583-e970a0ac913c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338618}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3cd142bb-0e37-5169-9871-c05d6282caa6" :question/math-academy-id "q-70974" :question/problem "Find a normal vector to the plane\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 12 \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,t,\\,s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨3,0,4⟩$ and $w=⟨1,-1,1⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =4i+j-3k \\\\  & =⟨4,1,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨4,1,-3⟩.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338864 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119935 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3061cb06-f57f-57c8-8821-dbd962b1e78e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametric Equation of the Plane Parallel To Two Lines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b6d3463-0771-5e04-b56b-54f54e1837a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,\\sqrt{2},-1⟩+s⟨1,2,-3⟩+t⟨-1,0,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336286} {:answer/id #uuid "2f58a87f-7c73-5da5-b8f8-e1aacaae0350" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,2,-3⟩+s⟨1,\\sqrt{2},-1⟩+t⟨-1,0,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336486} {:answer/id #uuid "4ae0deb5-2922-5529-9ad8-91ab2528ada9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r=⟨1,\\sqrt{2},-1⟩+s⟨0,11,\\frac{1}{3}⟩+t⟨0,\\sqrt{2},5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336722} {:answer/id #uuid "a223a9e3-d02c-5320-818f-d895e878dbc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident